Fixed Deposit Account: A fixed deposit is repayable after the
expiry of the specified period. The period may vary from six
months to five years. Longer the period of deposit, higher is
the rate of interest. The banks issue a receipt to the depositor
acknowledging the receipt called fixed deposit receipt. The
rate of interest in FD is highest.
Multiple Option Deposit Account: This account offers multiple
options to depositors. The account can be combination with
savings A/c or current A/c. In this account, the depositor can
enjoy the liquidity of savings and current A/c and rate of
interest of fixed deposit. When the amount of deposit
exceeds a particular limit then automatically the amount
transferred into fixed deposit.
